{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I was a rover on land and on [Am]sea
[Am]Till a good woman's [Em]love [G7]made a new man of [C]me
[C]Life had no meaning it was so [Am]incomplete
[Am]Till a good woman's [Em]love [G7]put me back on my [C]feet
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Stead [F]of roamin' I go home in the evening she's waiting [C]there
And [F]I know that no matter what happens she'll always [G7]care
And when the [C]night falls  and the moon shines [Am]above
I'm a man with a [Em]dream   [G7]and a good woman's [C]love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Solos
